{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1342141-dual-kith","id":1342141,"title":"Dual Kith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-18T11:45:49-07:00","id":1342141,"title":"Dual Kith","content":"Does anyone know if this merit exists, is going to exist in the future, or if there are any good homebrew creations out there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-18T12:52:11-07:00","id":1342154,"title":"","content":"It hasn't been updated to 2e, and it's unclear if it will.<br /> <br /> Dual Kith was kind of a problem Merit in 1e, esp. since the Kith bonuses were kind of all over the place in terms of usefulness/potency, and the Seeming-Kith link made it something of a concept tax as well.<br /> <br /> IME, you can tell something's probably not dialed in with a Merit when everyone comes to the table with a Dual Kith concept in mind (which has happened to me twice in 1e).<br /> <br /> Between the separation of Seeming and Kith, the current level of mechanical oomph for each, and 2e pushing for more homebrewed Kiths to cover concepts not in the current ones, Dual Kith seems unnecessary, as well as a problem in terms of pricing it out and possibly giving it a drawback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T00:05:40-07:00","id":1342481,"title":"","content":"While I don't know any good homebrews out 'there' I came up with this one just now, maybe it will work for you?<br /> <br /> Dual Kith (*-**)<br /> Prerequisite: Wyrd 2<br /> Your character benefits from the blessings of two different kiths. Upon taking this merit, you may select an additional kith, subject to ST restrictions. For 1 dot, your character gains the skill benefit of the second kith. For two dots, they benefit from the Trickery as well.<br /> <br /> I don't really think it's potent enough to need a drawback. If there was one, I'd say that Riddlekith had to be used twice to change both kiths or else just made the character a single kith (but that is a very niche drawback)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T11:44:23-07:00","id":1342768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1342141-dual-kith?p=1342481#post1342481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't know any good homebrews out 'there' I came up with this one just now, maybe it will work for you?<br /> <br /> Dual Kith (*-**)<br /> Prerequisite: Wyrd 2<br /> Your character benefits from the blessings of two different kiths. Upon taking this merit, you may select an additional kith, subject to ST restrictions. For 1 dot, your character gains the skill benefit of the second kith. For two dots, they benefit from the Trickery as well.<br /> <br /> I don't really think it's potent enough to need a drawback. If there was one, I'd say that Riddlekith had to be used twice to change both kiths or else just made the character a single kith (but that is a very niche drawback)</div> </div> </div> </div>No offence, but this is kind of delving right back into the same problems that 1e (and the Hill previews) had with Dual Kith - there\u2019s no reason <i>not</i> to take it. It\u2019s cheap even at maximum benefit, it has pretty big benefits (it\u2019s cheaper than a Contract of any variety with comparable benefit) and there is no drawback for taking it beyond having to be Wyrd 2. It also runs contrary to the general idea of making your own Kith to get the blessing you want.<br /> <br /> Even if a Kith may not seem big in 2e, it\u2019s a significant part of a Changeling, so having two Kiths active at once should likewise be a significant thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T19:41:41-07:00","id":1342854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1342141-dual-kith?p=1342768#post1342768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No offence, but this is kind of delving right back into the same problems that 1e (and the Hill previews) had with Dual Kith - there\u2019s no reason <i>not</i> to take it. It\u2019s cheap even at maximum benefit, it has pretty big benefits (it\u2019s cheaper than a Contract of any variety with comparable benefit) and there is no drawback for taking it beyond having to be Wyrd 2. It also runs contrary to the general idea of making your own Kith to get the blessing you want.<br /> <br /> Even if a Kith may not seem big in 2e, it\u2019s a significant part of a Changeling, so having two Kiths active at once should likewise be a significant thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No offense taken! Happy to hear your thoughts.<br /> <br /> It's cheaper than a contract because it's weaker than the contract of comparable benefit. The contract of comparable benefit you'd want to look at is the Riddle Kith Contract - which, with the Darkling Benefit, costs 1 Glamour to give you and anyone you target access to any kith abilities you like, including those you make yourself. Even for someone who wasn't a Darkling, and who didn't have Mirrors as a Favored Regalia, that's only 5 experience to get you an infinite pool of abilities to call upon for you and any friends you may have. In the most ideal situation of being a Darkling, it's a mere 1 experience more expensive than the merit - and 7 merit dots cheaper at creation. Which to me, seems like a solid reason -not- to get it: There is an easier, more effective option elsewhere - at least if you are just looking for a power boost.<br /> <br /> If you are looking for something to help build more complex concepts than a single kith allows, however - then the merit provides an avenue to do that. You could say that it runs contrary to the general idea of making your own kith to get the blessing you want - but really, we were always able to do that. You could still do that. Having Dual Kith doesn't really give me a reason not to make a fireheart, levinquick, or draconic. But I could still see the person who wanted to make a Levin-Drake making both Levinquick and Draconic, and taking both Levinquick and Draconic to fit their concept.<br /> <br /> Ultimately though, I don't think I saw original Dual Kith as the issue most people did either. Sure, there is no reason not to take it, and damn near everyone wants it and - like Heavy Arms mentioned - there are games where people come in and -everyone- has a concept with it in mind. But I can say the same thing about a merit like Striking Looks as well - least in a lot of my games. Everyone wanting a merit doesn't strike me as a flaw - it's everyone -needing- a merit that does. 1e had a flaw in which it was very challenging to make a great many concepts without the merit - which I will say 2e doesn't have. That alone should remove a lot of the -need- to use the merit when it is unnecessary to the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T21:14:29-07:00","id":1342867,"title":"","content":"The comparison to Riddlekith is a bit off simply because it has a cost, roll, and replaces Kith bonuses with the Darkling blessing, not grant you two. Dual Kith gives you two at a time, for no Glamour cost, that are both always on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T23:02:51-07:00","id":1342882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1342141-dual-kith?p=1342867#post1342867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The comparison to Riddlekith is a bit off simply because it has a cost, roll, and replaces Kith bonuses with the Darkling blessing, not grant you two. Dual Kith gives you two at a time, for no Glamour cost, that are both always on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the comparison is off at all. I never said that Riddle Kith gave you two kiths at once - But it does give you access to to other kiths - an infinite number of kiths, useful in as many situations as you could possibly think. The fact that they are not active at the same time doesn't really stop you from having access to them. The contract has an activation roll and cost, but in no way does any of these facts make the Dual Kith option even remotely close to as potent as the Royal Contract. <br /> <br /> It's the difference between you and your allies having access to what you need at any time, versus you having access to two things always that you might need depending on the situation.<br /> <br /> I think it's also a little misleading to state that Dual Kith provides the benefits of the kiths for no glamour costs and makes them always active. I think you are meaning to imply that they are both available to you at the same time, but the way you've written it makes it sound as though every kith currently <i>doesn't</i> have a glamour cost to activate their Trickery. If not, I apologize for misinterpreting and would appreciate a clarification.<br /> <br /> That said - those Trickeries do have a cost, and the only benefit that those kiths would provide 'at all times' would be that one or two skills would have more situations in which their threshold for success was reduced to three (which, wording-wise, would naturally not be stackable should the kith's skill benefits align).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T03:17:49-07:00","id":1343113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1342141-dual-kith?p=1342882#post1342882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I never said that Riddle Kith gave you two kiths at once...</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. I'm saying that to demonstrate why the comparison is off.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The contract has an activation roll and cost, but in no way does any of these facts make the Dual Kith option even remotely close to as potent as the Royal Contract. </div> </div> </div>OK.<br /> <br /> Lets say you have a stealth focused Kith, and the Stealth bonus applies to sneak attacks. You also have a grappling focused Brawling Kith. Classic ambush predator stuff.<br /> <br /> With Dual Kith, I get to use the Stealth boost (probably with the Trickery because of how ambushes work, as just getting an exceptional isn't necessarily enough), then I get to attack while ignoring Defense, and the reduced exceptional threshold is a big deal for grappling since you get to use two grapple maneuvers a turn if you exceptional (or in this case establish the grapple and apply a maneuver before the target gets to do anything.<br /> <br /> Darkling bonus boosted Riddlekith? It can't do that. If I've given myself the Stealthy ambushing Kith, I'd need to spend my turn swapping over to the Brawling grappler Kith... and then lose my ambush round.<br /> <br /> That's the sort of synergy that Dual Kith impacts, and Riddlekith doesn't. Riddlekith is insanely useful, but you can't switch rapidly, which can be a huge impact on faster moving scenes or when you've got both sides instigating contested rolls with different Skills. Not every situation is going to be one Skill oriented with time to swap bonuses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's the difference between you and your allies having access to what you need at any time,.. </div> </div> </div>I mean if you completely ignore how much Glamour that uses up, and the time it takes to use the Contract on each of your character's pals when under pressure. The Loophole for Riddlekith is not built to allow this sort of maximal utility without Glamour cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's also a little misleading to state that Dual Kith provides the benefits of the kiths for no glamour costs and makes them always active. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Additional&quot; Glamour costs, and the Skill aspect of their Blessing is always active, since you apparently need me to be highly pedantic to make this point to you.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T18:01:33-07:00","id":1343313,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">If I'm being honest - and I don't mean to be rude when I say this, which is ... honestly why I didn't say it to begin with - I felt you were already being pedantic when you made the comment about the comparison being off by contrasting it. That you can contrast something does not, in fact, invalidate that one serves as an appropriate comparison to the other for the purposes of determining cost effectiveness and usefulness.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The thing is, however, that I would <i>like</i> to see your point, and I would like to do so without needing to make a discussion an argument. The problem is - I... don't think I see your point.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The fact that Dual Kith would be allow you to use - as well as design - two kiths at once, that could be made to be synergistic with one another just... doesn't seem that big of an issue to me. The idea of building building a sheet with a kith designed to stalk your prey and have a high chance of succeeding on ambush and grapple to eat someone (Off Note: Gristlegrinders are awesome) not only doesn't sound like an issue to me - it sounds like a lot of fun, as well as a lot of work to make the character capable of doing that. I now have this image of everything being totally fine, and your character being one of those cute little wallflowers who just suddenly swallows your friend and everyone is going 'oh holy $#&amp;!'. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Similarly, that someone would either need to either prepare for the use of a reflexive contract use to be able to use two kiths synergistically, or else have to deal with the need to take a turn and pay the price of magic to change, seems more like a feature than a bug. In the scenario where both are available, it means that both have their uses. That the Contract requires a glamour cost to change yourself into whatever you like (as well as your allies and enemies, as the situation requires), and simply 'being an additional kith' would not, seems fair to me. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I'm not ignoring the fact that, if you chose to use your contract to be switching all sorts of people as you wished on the fly, that it would not be expensive. That it may very well fail because there is a roll on the contract and a merit would have the advantage of being a sure thing. The situation will change how you use it or what you use it for - which isn't really something you can say for Dual Kith. Once you take a Kith - and if your game permitted you to take a second one through whatever means you and your people chose to do (such as the homebrew merit above) - then the situation would tend to define <i>when</i> you could use it, rather than <i>how</i>. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T19:22:37-07:00","id":1343321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1342141-dual-kith?p=1343313#post1343313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">]The thing is, however, that I would <i>like</i> to see your point, and I would like to do so without needing to make a discussion an argument. The problem is - I... don't think I see your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems painfully obvious that this will devolve into an argument, because whatever you mean by wanting to see my point as it if was somehow not obvious from what I've said already, is because an argument would be necessary to challenge your clearly held and entrenched preconceptions.<br /> <br /> I've had this argument. Use the advanced search function, and look for me and Dual Kith. I and others made it so well Olivia Hill changed her version of Dual Kith from the design mentality that you replicated from 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-23T20:06:57-07:00","id":1343330,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000018\"><span style=\"font-family:BlinkMacSystemFont\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Eh. *shrugs* Whatever.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23573\" data-vbnamecard=\"23573\">ThriceHonored</a> This should be suitable. The one dot version allows a skill break, which is already replicated by at least 3 other merits that I can think of. It's not too much of a stretch to continue on the scale progression to 2 dots to gain access to the Trickery. If you are the ST, go forth and make awesome stories with awesome designs. If not, and your ST has the same or similar reservations as to what has been stated, consider making the Trickery require 3 dots, or giving it the drawback of an additional (or enhanced) frailty. Either way, it's a simple solution to a simple problem.<br /> <br /> P.S. If you could - let me know how it goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":".  Fixed @Thrice, Added Message 10-23-2019, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}